  "descriptionMarkdown": "The blueprint costs include only 289 space platforms (110 of which you start with - for a total of only 179 to send up in cargo rockets). Many resources are directly inserted into the hub and the science production occurs on a sushi belt. The system peaks out at 90 space science per minute, but it will likely average 80 science per minute in the long term due an ice bottleneck.\n\nThere are sets of inserters on the asteroid collectors that prevent them from backing up with carbon/iron asteroids.\n\nThere are no production or utility science pack requirements, so it can be used quite early in the tech tree.\n\nUpdate: Corrected an issue with the left-hand asteroid collector filling up.",
